  "description": "An Air Station Houston MH-65 Dolphin helicopter crew conducts a hoist of a 53-year-old man aboard the fishing vessel Fresh Catch who was suffering from possible decompression sickness 35 miles offshore of Freeport, Texas, Oct. 5, 2019. The diver was transferred to awaiting emergency medical services personnel at Memorial Hermann-Texas Medical Center and was reported to be in stable condition. (U.S. Coast Guard video by Air Station Houston)",
